Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:27:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pl18ev): support FlySky FRM301 as external AFHDS3 module

The FRM301 in the Paladin EV module bay uses the same port as the FRM303
but speaks the FlySkyOS variant of AFHDS3 (device address 2): the module
requests its configuration from the radio, uses different MODULE_MODE
values and keeps no bindings itself.

- detect FRM301/FRM303 automatically, or select the module type in the
  external module settings
- answer the module's requests (config parts 1-3, receiver block)
- bind like FlySkyOS: restart the module, push the config, store the
  receiver block (incl. receiver ID) returned by the module
- store receiver block and module options in the model (user data), so
  the receiver reconnects after a restart
- one way / two way selection, 2.5 ms frame period like FlySkyOS

Enabled by PL18EV_FRM301 (default ON).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
